# GitHub record of project work

- The user requires project work to be committed and pushed to GitHub.
- Before ending a work turn, commit completed code, tests, documentation,
  research decisions and relevant verification evidence, then push to origin.
- Use focused commits with clear messages and record scientific limitations.
- Respect .gitignore. Exclude credentials, environments, professor-supplied raw
  datasets, temporary downloads and scratch files.
- Verify the push and report the commit identifier. If a push is blocked,
  retain the local commit and explain the specific blocker.
